quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  34,32,"Those who were arrogant will say to those oppressed: ‘Did we hinder you from guidance after it had come to you? Instead, you were guilty (yourselves).’"
  34,33,"The oppressed will say to the arrogant: ‘No! (It was your) plotting by night and day when you prompted us to disbelieve in Allah and assign equals to Him.’ They will hide (their) regret when they see the punishment, and We will put iron shackles around the necks of the disbelievers. Will they be rewarded except for what they used to do?"
  34,34,"We never sent a warner to any town, but its elite would (always) say: ‘We reject what you have been sent with.’"
  34,35,"They said: ‘We have greater wealth and more children (than the believers), and we will never be punished.’"
  34,36,"Say: ‘Indeed, my Lord expands provision for whomever He pleases and tightens it (for whom He wills), but most people do not know.’"
  34,37,"It is not your wealth nor your children that will bring you closer to Our proximity. But those who believe and act righteously, it is they for whom there will be a manifold reward for what they did, and they will be secure in elevated mansions (of Paradise)."
  34,38,"As for those who strive to discredit Our revelations, seeking to undermine them, they will be brought to punishment."
  34,39,"Say: ‘Indeed, my Lord gives provision in abundance to whom He pleases among His servants and restraints it for whom (He wills). And whatever you spend (in charity), He will replace it (in compensation). And He is the best of providers.’"
